Slight correction: A confused blessed ?oRC[*] will randomly bless or 
curse any inventory object that's not already blessed or cursed. 
Here's one idea for getting unholy water with a b?oRC: 

1. Accrue as much uncursed water as possible.
2. #name the stack of water (and yes, you want to "Name an individual 
object").
3. Drop *one* potion from the stack, then rename the stack.
4. Repeat steps 1-3 until you have 51 #named uncursed waters (or 
however many were in the stack, if less). This is one of the more 
time-consuming parts.
5. In a safe place (preferrably a closet on a [semi-]permanent E-
square or ?oSM[+]), drop your entire inventory except the b?oRC.
6. Confuse yourself (an u!oB[#] works well here; alternatively, a 
non-orc, non-caveman can eat a tripe ration).
7. Pick up your named waters, and read the scroll.
8. Unname all of your water (just type in a space when it asks you 
for a name), drop it all, and pick it all up. Again, not difficuly, 
just time-consuming.

Hopefully you'll have three scks of water, which you can altar-test 
AFTER RE-EQUIPPING YOURSELF (if you have only two, determine whether 
it's all holy or unholy water, and repeat the above if it's holy).

NOTES
*: Scroll of remove curse
+: Scroll of scare monster
#: Uncursed potion of booze (yes, I specifically mean uncursed, not 
blessed)
